Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.00,0:00:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,In our house, breakfast was the time we\Nwere all together.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.50,0:00:14.80,Default,,0,0,0,,One morning, my mom and I started joking\Nabout the things my dad doesn't like.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.60,0:00:22.14,Default,,0,0,0,,We thought it was funny. He didn't\Nlaugh.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.60,0:00:28.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Upset, he got up and left the table\Nbefore finishing his breakfast.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.80,0:00:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,He washed his hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.50,0:00:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he came back and stood there\Nquietly, without a word.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.50,0:00:51.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we realised we had made him sad. We\Nsmiled and said sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.40,0:01:02.16,Default,,0,0,0,,He laughed, sat back down and started\Neating. Then he said:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.41,0:01:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,"I only came back because you said\Nsorry. I'm only eating for you!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.78,0:01:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,To this day, we laugh when we remember\Nit. Sometimes one 'sorry' is enough to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.59,0:01:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,bring someone back to the table.
